## Preserve non-OWL triples and external IRIs on OWL import

Context: GitHub #194 reported that OWL import rebuilt ontologies from the
Studio model, dropping SKOS, DCTERMS, PROV, and other annotations while
rewriting external parent references and replacing the ontology label.
Preserve graph metadata through the editable model without claiming
bit-exact Turtle text.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/w3c/owl/OntologyParser.py
   Preserve ontology metadata, language tags, full external references, and
   non-consumed triples during parsing.
2. src/back/core/w3c/owl/OntologyGenerator.py
   Restore preserved IRIs, namespaces, language tags, and RDF extras during
   OWL generation.
3. src/back/core/w3c/owl/OntologyRdfExtras.py
   Extract and safely reapply leftover ontology, class, and property triples.
4. src/back/objects/ontology/OntologyImport.py
   Persist parsed ontology identity, language metadata, and RDF extras in the
   active domain.
5. src/api/routers/internal/ontology.py
   Merge missing session RDF extras into Studio generate-OWL requests while
   retaining explicit request values.
6. docs/user-guide.md
   Document preserved OWL import metadata, deletion behavior, Studio limits,
   and the lack of bit-exact Turtle text preservation.
7. .planning/owl-import-fidelity/SPEC.md
   Define the fidelity scope, success criteria, and non-goals for GitHub #194.
8. .planning/owl-import-fidelity/PLAN.md
   Record the task-by-task implementation and verification plan.

