## Keep renamed OWL entities graph-consistent

Context: Whole-branch review found that stale imported IRIs could split renamed
classes and properties from their references. Slash namespaces were also
rewritten with a hash, and non-OWL import paths retained stale fidelity metadata.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/w3c/owl/OntologyGenerator.py
   Preserve slash namespace separators, reject stale stored IRIs after renames,
   and resolve constraints, axioms, groups, and relationship endpoints through
   the effective class/property subject IRIs.
2. src/back/objects/domain/Domain.py
   Preserve an imported ontology label and language metadata when saving domain
   information unless the ontology name was still derived from the domain name.
3. src/back/objects/ontology/OntologyImport.py
   Clear RDF extras and language metadata during RDFS and industry imports.
4. src/back/objects/session/DomainSession.py
   Clear RDF extras and language metadata when resetting the ontology.
5. tests/units/ontology/test_owl_generator.py
   Cover renamed class/property subjects, stale references, slash namespaces,
   and effective IRIs in constraints, axioms, and groups.
6. tests/units/ontology/test_ontology_service.py
   Cover fidelity metadata cleanup for RDFS and industry imports.
7. tests/units/domain/test_domain_service.py
   Cover imported ontology label preservation during domain saves.
8. tests/units/domain/test_domain_session.py
   Cover fidelity metadata cleanup during ontology reset.

